WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.180
ALICIA WILLIAMS:
Today we're talking

00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:06.140
about data sets, BigQuery,
and managing VMs.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.690
I'm Alicia, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:13.290
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.360
With Google Cloud's
datasets, you

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.780
can access an ever-expanding
collection of data to support

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.080
and empower your
analyses and ML models.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.320
The most recent addition is
all of Google Cloud's release

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.070
notes.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:29.010
Make sure you bookmark this
blog post, because we're

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.770
keeping it up to date
with dataset news and best

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.510
practices.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.610
Interested in checking
out those datasets

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.650
but aren't quite
sure where to start?

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:40.800
Leah has been busy bringing
us all kinds of tips

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:43.620
on how to architect and
administer BigQuery.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.530
Whether you're new to BigQuery
or just looking to brush up,

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:51.900
these blogs and videos will help
you become a BigQuery expert.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:55.620
The cloud is full of new and
exciting technologies which

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:58.110
can help you innovate and save.

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.810
We just published a full
guide of different ways

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:02.970
to help you manage
your virtual machines

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:05.129
and save some
money by not paying

00:01:05.129 --> 00:01:07.500
for resources you're not using.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.300
From simply pausing
machines that

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.610
aren't needed to
building an automated

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.970
solution with Recommender,
find the best way to optimize

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:18.330
your usage with this guide.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:21.420
If you're building an app and
need a relational database,

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.310
Cloud SQL has what you need.

00:01:23.310 --> 00:01:27.570
It's a fully managed relational
database for MySQL, PostgreSQL

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:28.920
and SQL Server.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.350
And if you're looking for
some tips on how it works

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.600
or how to migrate, check
out these resources

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.087
from Priyanka and Gabe.

00:01:36.087 --> 00:01:38.170
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:40.730
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:42.130
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:42.130 --> 00:01:44.300
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:46.920
We'll see you in the Cloud.

